RF.put("questb:b71",{"8711":{"id":8711,"t":"Blade of Eternal Justice","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Spiked Hilt, 2 Amber Idols, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Warden Haro in Silithus. You must also attain Exalted reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Spiked Hilt Ossirian the Unscarred 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Amber Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 42000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The Qiraji and their servants wield items made with the rarest and finest materials: bones from gargantuan ancient creatures, gems from the depths of the earth, metals pure and strong.\nJust the sight of Qiraji artifacts fills me with an urge to practice my craft with their shattered and smelted pieces. Prove your allegiance to the Circle, ‹name›, and I will make you a powerful weapon from the finest Qiraji materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nBlade of Eternal Justice\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the components I require, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹class›. This is a masterwork hilt... the balance is perfect.\nTake your weapon, ‹name›. Wield it with great confidence and vanquish our enemies!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.1,"y":38.9,"n":"Warden Haro","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8631":{"id":8631,"t":"Enigma Leggings","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ouro's Intact Hide, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nOuro's Intact Hide Ouro\n2 Idol of the Sage Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"You seek to prove your worth to my kind, mortal? Very well, perhaps we can be of mutual assistance.\nThe ancient sandworm, Ouro, is a being of legendary power. He is rumored to have been created by the Old God himself as a mockery of life.\nHis skin is unnatural... thick, nearly impregnable, yet it's flexible and allows him to move with the speed and grace of a much smaller creature.\nBring me a sample of his skin along with other minor components and I shall craft you leggings of great power.","rew":"You will receive:\nEnigma Leggings\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Mage Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8631\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Enigma Leggings this quest\nBring Ouro's Intact Hide, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"551":{"id":551,"t":"The Ensorcelled Parchment","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Ensorcelled Parchment to Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore.\nEnsorcelled Parchment Worn Wooden Chest\nProvided: Ensorcelled Parchment","desc":"This parchment is enchanted with a spell, rendering it indecipherable. But one word at the top of the paper can be read:\nNagaz","rew":"Experience: 775","back":"Oh. You have something you'd like me to look at? Some scrap of lore gathered from up in the mountains, I hope...","done":"More encrypted notes?\nI wish I had the talents to decrypt all the strange bits of writing that trickle down from Alterac. But I'm afraid I lack the knowledge.\nAlterac Mountains Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":39.2,"y":14.7,"n":"Ensorcelled Parchment","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":50.6,"y":57.1,"n":"Loremaster Dibbs","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"99191":{"id":99191,"t":"A donation of wool","lv":60,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"60 Wool Cloth","back":"The High Order are currently accepting donations for wool cloth.\nA donation of sixty pieces of wool cloth will net you full recognition by the High Order for your generous actions. Sixty pieces of wool should prove to be a sufficient amount for the High Order's needs for now.\nIf you have the sixty pieces of wool cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.\nWool Cloth (60)","done":"Wonderful!\nWe thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":11.6,"y":57.8,"n":"Belanaa Windveil","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"8391":{"id":8391,"t":"Claiming Arathi Basin","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Winning a war is about more than just outsmarting and outfighting your opponent. Victory often comes down to simply producing more than your enemy.\nWhat we have in Arathi Basin is a sizeable supply of resources for whichever side manages to claim it first.\nIf the Alliance comes out victorious, it'll mean more swords and pikes for our troops. If the Horde were to win, those swords and pikes would still get made, they'd just be pointed at us! Now is the time to help the Alliance in Arathi Basin, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 1,500\n+50 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Tell me, what are the news from the front?","done":"Good work, soldier! Keep it up and we'll have the Horde running all the way back to Orgrimmar.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"1031":{"id":1031,"t":"The Branch of Cenarius","lv":32,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Geltharis and return the Branch of Cenarius to Illiyana at Forest Song.\nBranch of Cenarius Geltharis , Prince Raze","desc":"Anilia puts her hands on your shoulders and draws you close. Gasping, she points towards the arch to the north, before her eyes close and her last wheezing breath leaves her body. \"He has taken it... Geltharis...\" You know in your heart that Anilia's dying wish is to see the Branch of Cenarius back in dryad hands.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFaerie Mantle Brightscale Girdle\nExperience: 2,550\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Have you found them? What did Anilia say? Where is she?","done":"Anilia died? No... that can't be! It was just yesterday that we were running and playing together in the woods.\nI guess those days are over...","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":78.3,"y":44.8,"n":"Anilia","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":21.7,"y":53.3,"n":"Illiyana","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3511":{"id":3511,"t":"The Name of the Beast","lv":58,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the temper back to Loramus Thalipedes.\nHetaera's Blood\nProvided: Hetaera's Blood","desc":"As promised, I will reveal the name of the demon lord, Razelikh the Defiler. First, however, I must prepare something of utmost importance for your journey.\nThe weapon you seek to create requires a temper. Give me a moment to drain the blood from these heads.\n<Lord Arkkoroc squeezes the heads in between his gigantic fists, draining them of their blood.>\nTake the temper back to Loramus along with the name of the beast: Rakh'likh.","rew":"Experience: 3,100","back":"You return! Astounding, ‹race›. Did you discover the true name?","done":"The temper will add the necessary vitriol we require for the forging of the weapons. There is but one more step in their creation.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":77.1,"y":42.8,"n":"Lord Arkkoroc","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":60.8,"y":66.4,"n":"Loramus Thalipedes","e":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"711":{"id":711,"t":"Study of the Elements: Rock","lv":39,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Large Stone Slabs to Lotwil Veriatus in the Badlands.\n3 Large Stone Slab Rock Elemental 80 %","desc":"‹name›, you've already proven more able than all my apprentices combined.\nThe next parts I need require a little more strength. Large stone slabs can be found on rock elementals if you're careful enough. Their bodies are stronger and larger, and therefore more prone to having pieces large enough for my tests. You can find them further west of here or southeast along the mountains' edges.\nTake your time; I'll need a while to test these smaller pieces you brought me.","rew":"Experience: 3,000","back":"I'm most pleased, ‹name›. My spells affected the smaller pieces just as I predicted. If this experiment is as successful as I foresee, then the elementals I'll be able to control will put anything summoned prior to this to shame.","done":"‹name›, simply amazing! I would have thought it'd take half a dozen tauren to bring all these to me.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":25.9,"y":44.9,"n":"Lotwil Veriatus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"3911":{"id":3911,"t":"The last element","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Depths and recover 10 Essence of the Elements. Your first inclination is to search the golems and golem makers. You remember Vivian Lagrave also muttering something about elementals.\n10 Essence of the Elements","desc":"There is work to be had for those venturing into the depths, ‹name›.\nThe Dark Irons have mastered creation of extremely powerful golems.\nInitial reports from our spies indicate that the dwarves use a unique power source to give their creations incomparable killing power.\nJust imagine what we could do with our abominations if we could get our hands on this essence of the elements! Turn that city upside down if you must, but do not return until you have found the essence! Payment will be worth the risk.","rew":"You will receive:\nLagrave's Seal\nMoney: 2 45 2 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,450\n+100 reputation with Undercity\nLevel 54 , requires level 48 Difficulty 48 50 52 57 Side Both factions Type Elite Shareable Yes Quest ID 3911","cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"94231":{"id":94231,"t":"Craftsmans writ moonsight rifle","min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Moonsight Rifle\nMoonsight Rifle","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Moonsight Rifle, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Hey, HEY, man, haven't you heard of a little thing called \"subtlety\"? Spell it out with me, S-U-B...LETY. You're going to blow my cover!","done":"Ohoho, I take it back. Look at this beautiful boomstick. I bet it'll knock a satyr's head clean off.\nThanks pal, now step aside or you're going to get caught in the crossfire.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":82.2,"y":51,"n":"Grembly","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94311":{"id":94311,"t":"Craftsmans writ red mageweave pants","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Red Mageweave Pants\nRed Mageweave Pants","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Red Mageweave Pants, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Red Mageweave Pants Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94311","cats":["crafting"]},"951":{"id":951,"t":"Mathystra Relics","lv":20,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Mathystra Relics to Onu at the Grove of the Ancients.\n6 Mathystra Relic Mathystra Relic , Mathystra Relic , Mathystra Relic","desc":"The parchment you found at the Master's Glaive is a page from an ancient text...written by elves! It is heavily cursed and tainted by the corruption of the Twilight's Hammer, but it seems the cult is using ancient elven magic to bring their old masters back to our world.\nTravel to the ruins of Mathystra to the northeast, and search for ancient relics among the grass and broken stones. Through their study, we may divine how the Twilight's Hammer intends to exploit the magic of the elves.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHardwood Cudgel Woodsman Sword\nExperience: 1,950\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"‹name›. Has your rooting through the Ruins of Mathystra been fruitful?","done":"Thank you. These relics are from a time when Mathystra shone. That once great bastion of the elves has faded, but shards of its magic remain. Let us hope we can unlock the secrets of that place before our enemies...\nBe vigilant, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":43.6,"y":76.3,"n":"Onu","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"7671":{"id":7671,"t":"Frostsaber Replacement","lv":1,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Reins of the Frostsaber","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nReins of the Swift Stormsaber Reins of the Swift Frostsaber Reins of the Swift Mistsaber","back":"[PH] If you bring me your old frostsaber, I will trade it in for one from the new pack. The new swift saber will be just as fast as your old one, but have a different look to it. You can look at the swift sabers we already have around the yard here to see what it will look like.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":38.3,"y":15.4,"n":"Lelanai","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"98391":{"id":98391,"t":"The sisterhood of elune","lv":10,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Sister Aquinne in Darnassus.","desc":"Blessings to you, ‹class›. The Sisterhood of Elune has stood as a pillar of kaldorei society for thousands of years.\nBefore the Great Sundering, before the War of the Ancients, through the Long Vigil, we have guided and healed our people through the darkness. Such is our charge, and such is the demand of the peerless Mother Moon.\nWe now require your aid in a matter of great importance. Sister Aquinne awaits your arrival in Darnassus.","done":"I am glad you arrived so quickly. The Sisterhood requires your aid.\nTeldrassil Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.6,"y":56.8,"n":"Laurna Morninglight","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":29,"y":45.4,"n":"Sister Aquinne","e":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"311":{"id":311,"t":"Return to Marleth","lv":7,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the barrel of Thunder Ale to Marleth Barleybrew at the Brewnall Village.\nBarrel of Thunder Ale\nProvided: Barrel of Thunder Ale","desc":"Having inserted a barrel of Marleth's Scalder in the Kharanos Distillery's cellar, you grab a barrel of Thunder Ale as proof of the deed...","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Did you make the switch?","done":"Not bad, ‹name›! Did you have a hard time getting past their guard?\nNo matter - many thanks, and if you're ever in need of stout with a kick, don't forget the Barleybrews!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.7,"y":52.7,"n":"Unguarded Thunder Ale Barrel","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":30.2,"y":45.5,"n":"Marleth Barleybrew","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"96391":{"id":96391,"t":"Underground map","lv":15,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver the Dark Iron Map to Earthseer Farsen in Dun Morogh.\nProvided: Dark Iron Map","desc":"<The map you are holding seems to show a complex series of underground tunnels and highways that all seem to converge on a point underneath Ironforge itself.\nYou can't be sure what the runes say as they are written in the ugly jagged rune language of the Dark Iron dwarves, but you can guess at the purpose of these tunnels. As you are reading the map, a gust of wind washes over you and you can faintly hear a dwarven voice carried on it. Earthseer Farsen needs to see this.>","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Oh what's this, then?","done":"Juding by this map, it certainly looks like these Dark Irons are planning some sort of incursion into the vaults beneath Ironforge. The band ye busted up to the east must be a scouting force.\nThank ye for bringing me this. If we hurry, we might be able to beat them to whatever their goal is down there.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":64.8,"y":58.4,"n":"Earthseer Farsen","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"791":{"id":791,"t":"Carry Your Weight","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Furl Scornbrow in the Razor Hill watchtower wants 8 Canvas Scraps.\n8 Canvas Scraps Warlord Kolkanis 30 % , Watch Commander Zalaphil 30 % , Lieutenant Benedict 30 % , Kul Tiras Marine 30 % and 3 more","desc":"Age has rendered me useless in battle. Now I make myself useful in other ways.\nFrom this vantage point I watch for invaders. As our strength here grows, I find myself blowing the signal horn less and less.\nTo pass the time I fashion goods to help younger, more able warriors defend our homeland.\nFor you, I can fashion you a bag for your belongings. If such an item would be of use to you, bring me some canvas, a material common to the humans and centaurs.","rew":"You will receive:\nHandmade Leather Bag\nExperience: 625\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"I fought proudly alongside the Warchief when these lands were pioneered. The scars of battle mark my skin.\nThe honor of the Horde has been upheld with the help of my axe and battlecry during the defeat of Archimonde, when the unholy alliance was made with the humans and elves, wrought from necessity.\nBut my position as watchman and provider has given me a new sense of worth.","done":"Most excellent, ‹name›. Any good ‹class› will surely find a use for this bag on the battlefield.\nI salute your vigor and willingness to die in the name of the Horde!","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":49.9,"y":40.4,"n":"Furl Scornbrow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"231":{"id":231,"t":"A Daughter's Love","lv":35,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Ladimore Heirloom Ring.","obj":"Take Sarah Ladimore's ring to Morgan Ladimore's grave.\nSarah's Ring\nProvided: Sarah's Ring","desc":"Here, take this and lay it on his grave. Maybe... somehow, he'll know that I'm okay, and that none of us hold him responsible for what happened.\n<There are tears in her eyes now, as she slides a ring from her right hand, and presses it into your hands.>\nAnd... thank you, ‹name›.","rew":"New in Forever: Ladimore Heirloom Ring.\nYou will receive:\nArcheus Ladimore Heirloom Ring\nExperience: 1,350","back":"Leave me be...","done":"<A ghostly voice sounds on the wind...>\nThis is...? Sarah? Could it be she's still alive? The weight is removed from my shoulders...\n‹name›. Take my sword, Archeus. As my soul is put to rest, I have no more need for it. It was forged to do good, and though I have proved myself unworthy to hold it, perhaps you will carry on the Light through it.\nLys, my love...","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":74,"y":47.8,"n":"Watcher Ladimore","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":17.7,"y":29.1,"n":"A Weathered Grave","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1271":{"id":1271,"t":"Feast at the Blue Recluse","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nMoist Towelette","done":"My nephew said you aided him with his research in Dustwallow, and that you helped his associate out of a tight spot. Well, we Sterns stick together and we don't ignore our friends!\nSo wash your hands, ‹name›, because we're about to throw a party in your honor!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.8,"y":93.6,"n":"Angus Stern","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"9191":{"id":9191,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Runecloth Bag","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 8 Runecloth Bags and the Craftsman's Writ - Runecloth Bag - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Runecloth Bag\n8 Runecloth Bag\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Runecloth Bag","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order TR-9999:\n8 Runecloth Bags.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"Blessed bootstraps! Are those what I think they are? The troops have been complaining non-stop about the lack of storage space for all that is required while in the field. One of them even drew me a diagram - such a pansy...\nThese will definitely help alleviate some of the whining.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"91751":{"id":91751,"t":"Rough wolf pelts","lv":7,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Skin wolves around Elwynn Forest to obtain 7 Rough Wolf Pelts, then deliver them to Helene Peltskinner near Goldshire.\n7 Rough Wolf Pelt","desc":"Are you looking for an opportunity to practice skinning? My husband usually helps with hunting wolves, but he's busy up by the abbey. I could use a hand collecting more pelts to finish the orders I'm working on.","rew":"Money: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 480\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Any luck with those wolf pelts?","done":"Excellent work collecting these pelts, ‹class›. You have a real talent for hunting.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":46.2,"y":62.2,"n":"Helene Peltskinner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"71":{"id":71,"t":"Report to Thomas","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Rolf and Malakai's Medallions to Guard Thomas at the eastern Elwynn bridge.\nRolf and Malakai's Medallions Murloc Streamrunner 40 % , Murloc Raider 40 % , Murloc Forager 40 %\nProvided: Rolf and Malakai's Medallions","desc":"Now that you have both medallions, deliver them to Guard Thomas at the bridge so that he might know the fate of his murdered guards.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Have you discovered the fates of Rolf and Malakai?","done":"You have confirmed my fears, ‹name›. The murlocs are a threat we cannot ignore.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":79.8,"y":55.5,"n":"Rolf's corpse","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":74,"y":72.2,"n":"Guard Thomas","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"2871":{"id":2871,"t":"Delivering the Relic","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Mysterious Relic to Vestia Moonspear in Feathermoon Stronghold.\nMysterious Relic Lord Shalzaru\nProvided: Mysterious Relic","desc":"If you would be so kind as to deliver the relic to my wife Vestia, I would appreciate it. She's not only a fine priestess for our community, but she is one of the most well-versed scholars you'll find anywhere. I couldn't make heads or tails of this device even if there was a wager involved. My wife though, if anyone can figure out what this thing is, she could... and we need to know!\nShe's just around the bend, no doubt studying. Thanks, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDawnrider's Chestpiece Sentinel's Guard\nExperience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Yes, may I assist you?\nHold on, you're the ‹class› that has been helping General Feathermoon and Latro out with the naga threat, yes? I'm Vestia, Latro's - erm, rather, Latronicus' wife. It is a pleasure to meet you!\nI'm sorry, you're here on business, of course. Do you have something for me - from him, perchance?","done":"Interesting... this came from the Ruins of Solarsal, you say? Well, Latro's right that I need to look at this. At first glance, it seems non-indigenous to the ruins. Then again, this isn't of naga design... not something as alien as this.\nIt is going to take some time to research this item. Once my research on it is done, maybe I will make use of your talents, should you be around.\nHere, take one of these extra items we have; I hope you'll find some use for it!","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.4,"y":46.2,"n":"Latronicus Moonspear","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":30.1,"y":45.1,"n":"Vestia Moonspear","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2951":{"id":2951,"t":"The Sparklematic 5200!","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -1g -3s instead of 0.","obj":"Insert a Grime-Encrusted Item into the Sparklematic 5200, and be sure to have three silver coins to start the machine.\nGrime-Encrusted Object Holdout Technician 25 % , Holdout Medic 25 % , Holdout Warrior 25 % , Irradiated Pillager 25 % and 4 more","desc":"This contraption stands out amongst the gnomes holding out against the madness outside the room. A small plaque on the device reads \"The Sparklematic 5200\", followed by some text:\n\"Grime and residue ruining your sparklies? The Sparklematic 5200 puts the shine back in shine-tastic! Insert the item you wish to clean and deposit three silver coins in the coin slot. Give the Sparklematic 5200 a moment for operation, and voila! Your valuables will emerge clean and shiny!\"","back":"It would seem that the device needs some sort of grime-encrusted object to clean and three silver coins to get the contraption working. So long as both are present, the Sparklematic 5200 should work...","done":"You insert the grime-encrusted item and three silver coins into the Sparklematic 5200. The machine surges to life in a frenzied attempt to purge the grime from the unknown item. Loud, violent churning sounds beat from the heart of the machine. The metal frame of the beast creaks and groans as it lurches from side to side...\nStart The Sparklematic 5200 End The Sparklematic 5200 Level 30 , requires level 25 Difficulty 25 26 28 33 38 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 2951\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 30, 2,450 XP in all.\n1 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200! this quest\nInsert a Grime-Encrusted Item into the Sparklematic 5200, and be sure to have three silver coins to start the machine.\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200!\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2,450 XP\n3 [ 30 ] More Sparklematic Action\nThe Sparklematic 5200","cats":["gnomeregan"]},"98071":{"id":98071,"t":"Brewers trade","lv":27,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver the bottles of Fallrook Varietal to Dun Garok in southeast Hillsbrad Foothills, and bring back a sack of their Homebrew Hops.\nFallrook Varietal delivered to Dun Garok\nSack of Homebrew Hops","desc":"Worked a bit o' a trade with the Dun Garok brew-kin. We're not the only ones missin' the vineyards of the Fallrook family, it seems! Most o' the best bottled years are long since drank, but we do have cases of the wine still in the cellars.\nBring this case of Fallrook Varietal to Dun Garok in the southeast and leave it with 'em by their gatherin' fireplace at the bottom of their fort.\nIn return, carry a sack o' the Homebrew Hops back with ye.\nThat keep is the closest thing to home around here!","rew":"You will receive:\nBrewer's Bracers\nMoney: 11 0 gold, 11 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,200","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":52,"y":58.6,"n":"Brewmeister Bilger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6071":{"id":6071,"t":"The Hunter's Path","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Dazalar in Dolanaar.","desc":"Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.\nYou must see Dazalar in Dolanaar. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Yes, it is time, ‹class›.\nDarnassus Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":40.4,"y":8.5,"n":"Jocaste","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.7,"y":59.5,"n":"Dazalar","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"8151":{"id":8151,"t":"The Hunter's Charm","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Ogtinc in Azshara.","desc":"Ogtinc of Azshara has sent out a call for seasoned hunters such as yourself. He is a furbolg hunter who has left his tribe to aid the Cenarion Circle. His teachings are meant to enrich the wisdom of others who share his craft, and guide them toward maintaining a balance. You would do well to speak with him.\nOgtinc resides atop the cliffs of Azshara, northeast from the Ruins of Eldarath.","rew":"Experience: 500","done":"It is no longer my purpose to hunt, but to teach the ‹class›. That is what fate has handed to me.\nCraft with me a ‹class›'s charm -- a collection of trophies from fallen prey that will remind you of your past trials and triumphs. In the end I will keep the charm, but reward you with something else.\nThunder Bluff Orgrimmar Darnassus Dun Morogh Stormwind City Azshara","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":58.5,"y":88.3,"n":"Kary Thunderhorn","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":67.2,"y":20.2,"n":"Xor'juul","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":42.2,"y":7.3,"n":"Dorion","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.5,"y":34.5,"n":"Olmin Burningbeard","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":67.6,"y":35.8,"n":"Ulfir Ironbeard","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":42.4,"y":42.6,"n":"Ogtinc","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"8231":{"id":8231,"t":"Wavethrashing","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Wavethrasher Scales to Ogtinc in Azshara. Ogtinc resides atop the cliffs northeast the Ruins of Eldarath.\n6 Wavethrasher Scales Young Wavethrasher 31.8 % , Wavethrasher 29 % , Great Wavethrasher 15.2 %","desc":"The wavethrasher is an amphibious beast living only here in Azshara. They are powerful and resilient.\nThe tough, reflective scales from a wavethrasher mirror the strength of the hunter.\nTrack and hunt wavethrashers along the coast of Azshara, and bring me their scales.","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"Have you met with success?","done":"The wavethrashers are not easily defeated, even more so in their watery environment.\nYou have proven yourself ready to hunt even deadlier prey.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":42.4,"y":42.6,"n":"Ogtinc","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"98471":{"id":98471,"t":"Message from the supreme magister","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Meet Elaadrin Evengale at the cliffs overlooking The Uplands in Alterac Mountains.\nProvided: Message from the Supreme Magister","desc":"Greetings, ‹name›.\nI have an assignment for you that is of the utmost priority. Please meet me in the mountains called Alterac, northwest of the village known as Strahnbrad. I will meet you at the cliff overlooking the Uplands valley.\nCome alone, and tell no one.\nStart an item: Message from the Supreme Magister Level 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Alliance Quest ID 98471","cats":["invasion"]},"8951":{"id":8951,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Deliana in Ironforge with a set of Wildheart Boots, a Wildheart Kilt and Wildheart Spaulders.\nWildheart Boots Mother Smolderweb 15 %\nWildheart Kilt Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nWildheart Spaulders Gizrul the Slavener 15 %\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the medallion back together. Return to Deliana and tell her that Bodley is her only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to her about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nFeralheart Boots Feralheart Kilt Feralheart Spaulders\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're back, ‹name›. You must tell me all about what you've found out. But first let us arrange for your reward.","done":"I can't believe our lives are all but forfeit all because of a stupid medallion! And you're sure Anthion mentioned Bodley?\nWell, you've done your job so let's get your reward out of the way.\nEastern Plaguelands Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"9271":{"id":9271,"t":"Atiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 14,300, 0.7 times as much.","obj":"Anachronos at the Caverns of Time in Tanaris wants you to take Atiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian to Stratholme and use it on Consecrated Earth. Defeat the entity that is exorcised from the staff and return to him.\nAtiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian\nAtiesh Cleansed\nProvided: Atiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian","desc":"This final task will be the most difficult of all, ‹name›. You have faced and defeated both an Old God and the Lich King's General, but now you must face the hand of Sargeras.\nTake the staff to Stratholme. It is there that you will find a piece of consecrated earth: ground where the greatest knights of Lordaeron were murdered. Place the befouled staff upon the holy ground and prepare for an entity of immense power to break from within... Defeat the demonic being that controls the staff and return to me.","rew":"You will receive:\nAtiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["legendary"]},"6391":{"id":6391,"t":"Ride to Ironforge","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Buy a gryphon to Ironforge from the gryphon master Thorgrum Borrelson, then bring Brock's List to Golnir Bouldertoe in Ironforge.\nBrock's List\nProvided: Brock's List","desc":"For just a few coins, one of my gryphons will take you to Ironforge. From there, deliver Brock's list to Golnir Bouldertoe. You'll find him in the Deep Mountain Mining Guild. That's in the Great Forge District of Ironforge, which is right where my gryphon will drop you off!\nSpeak to me again when you're ready for the journey.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Ironforge\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"What can I do for you, sir?","done":"Ah, the lastest list of Brock's best pupils. I have a batch of honorary picks ready to go. I just need to chisel in the names of the students...\nLoch Modan Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":33.9,"y":51,"n":"Thorgrum Borrelson","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.4,"y":25.3,"n":"Golnir Bouldertoe","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8871":{"id":8871,"t":"The Lunar Festival","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to the Lunar Festival Harbinger in the Park District in Stormwind. You can also talk to Lunar Festival Harbingers in other capital cities.","desc":"It's that time of the year, ‹name›! The Cenarion Circle invites all denizens of Azeroth to partake in our celebration of the Lunar Festival. You will find the Lunar Festival Harbinger in this very city at a location marked by a blessed circle of moonlight. She can tell you more about the holiday.","done":"Welcome, ‹name›. Are you here to join in the festivities?\nStormwind City Dun Morogh Darnassus Tirisfal Glades Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.1,"y":64.7,"n":"Lunar Festival Emissary","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.9,"y":24,"n":"Lunar Festival Emissary","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":31.2,"y":12.5,"n":"Lunar Festival Emissary","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.7,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":41.7,"y":32,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":71.1,"y":28.2,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9111":{"id":9111,"t":"Robe of Faith","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Robe of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Robe, 25 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 4 Mooncloth and 2 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Robe\n25 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Mooncloth\n2 Nexus Crystal","desc":"<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\nBlessed boy/girl, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.","rew":"You will receive:\nRobe of Faith\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Robe of Faith.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Father Inigo Montoy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"1431":{"id":1431,"t":"Alliance Relations","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Keldran in Orgrimmar.","desc":"Be still, ‹class›, and allow me to share with you something important to our people, but far from obvious.\nWe are a proud race, and the war with the humans tried even Thrall's great patience. You see, our Warchief is wise and prudent, and he continues to put his people first. Ultimately, he is a diplomat, and in his time with the humans he learned much of their ways.\nIf the tale I've started piques your interest, then find Keldran near the western exit of the city. His hovel is there.","rew":"Experience: 600\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"‹name›, noble ‹class›. I am Keldran, student of magic... and other mystical arts.\nThe business Craven sent you here to speak to me about requires a touch more subtlety than you've previously needed, but that does not mean you can not still aid our cause.\nPlease, make yourself comfortable, and I shall tell you why the Warchief has need of my aid... and yours.\nIt starts with appearances, ‹name›. How the Horde sees itself. How our allies see us. And most importantly, how our enemies see us.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":45.7,"y":49.9,"n":"Craven Drok","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":22.6,"y":52.6,"n":"Keldran","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"7831":{"id":7831,"t":"A Donation of Mageweave","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Mageweave Cloth Northshire Guard 54.5 % , Deep Dweller 48.4 % , Refuge Pointe Defender 40.7 % , Stonard Hunter 40.2 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Mageweave is running low, and we could use your help to replenish our stocks! By counting on the community as a whole, we would only need a donation of 60 pieces of mageweave cloth from you to enable us to reach our goal. Such generosity would not go unnoticed by Orgrimmar, I assure you!\nIf you have the sixty pieces of mageweave cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":63.6,"y":51.2,"n":"Rashona Straglash","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"95111":{"id":95111,"t":"An underrated talent","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Ott and ask him to forge your blade.\nProvided: Bundle of Blacksmithing Materials","desc":"In Tarren Mill there is a weaponsmith known as Ott. By all accounts he is an unremarkable smith, selling simple blades to travelers. I purchased a sword from him myself, and when I took it to the undercity for maintenance some time later, the smiths there were surprised at its quality. They assumed it came from a well known master smith, but no, it was just Ott.\nI'd like to give this orc a chance to do something truly special. Take the materials to Ott in Tarren Mill and offer him the commission.","back":"Are you in need of a blade, ‹class›?","done":"Interesting. I don't think anyone has ever asked me to actually carry out a custom commission for them. Mostly I just make humble, functional weapons in my own style. It's not much, but its honest work and I don't seek accolades or glory.\nI'm happy to try, but why would you seek me for this? There are plenty of smiths in the Undercity that will take on custom jobs like this.\nSilverpine Forest Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":41,"n":"Trevan Rol","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":60.4,"y":26,"n":"Ott","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"8791":{"id":8791,"t":"The Fall of Ossirian","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Head of Ossirian the Unscarred to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.\nHead of Ossirian the Unscarred Ossirian the Unscarred in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\nProvided: Head of Ossirian the Unscarred","desc":"A terrible menace has been laid to rest. The cruel Ossirian has been vanquished.\nThe denizens of Kalimdor would be relieved to know of this victory. Take Ossirian's head and present it to Commander Mar'alith of Cenarion Hold.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCharm of the Shifting Sands Amulet of the Shifting Sands Choker of the Shifting Sands Pendant of the Shifting Sands\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Cenarion Circle\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Ah, ‹name›, you have returned! And in one piece, I might add. What news do you bring from Ahn'Qiraj?","done":"I offer you my highest commendation and your choice of an item of power, ‹name›. You have done the people of Kalimdor a great service.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["ruins-of-ahnqiraj"]},"8311":{"id":8311,"t":"Hallow's End Treats for Jesper!","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with the innkeepers of Stormwind, Ironforge, and Darnassus, as well as Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge. Perform the tricks they ask of you in exchange for the treats they offer.\nReturn to Jesper at the Stormwind Orphanage with a Darnassus Marzipan, Gnomeregan Gumdrop, Stormwind Nougat, and Ironforge Mint.\nStormwind Nougat\nGnomeregan Gumdrop\nIronforge Mint\nDarnassus Marzipan","desc":"I want to go trick-or-treating, but I can't because I'm sick. If you go for me, I'd trade you the candy you get for some I already have! I think you'd like this candy - it makes you turn into things both funny and scary!\nEach of the innkeepers in the big cities have candy they give for Hallow's End - talk to them and do the tricks they ask for! Also, a little gnome named Talvash in Ironforge is handing out candy as well. When you have all the candy, bring them back to me here!","rew":"You will receive:\n30 Hallow's End Pumpkin Treat\nExperience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Alliance","back":"Have you finished trick-or-treating yet? I'm sad that I can't go because I'm sick, but you helping me out makes me feel a little better...","done":"Wow, you got them all! You're awesome!\nThank you for trick-or-treating for me. Here, take these pumpkin treats - I think you'll like them a lot!\nHappy Hallow's End, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":56.5,"y":51.8,"n":"Jesper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8551":{"id":8551,"t":"The Captain's Chest","lv":47,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 35 instead of 40.","obj":"Bring Smotts' Chest to Hecklebury Smotts in Booty Bay.\nSmotts' Chest Gorlash","desc":"I used to sail a ship from here all the way to Ratchet, in Kalimdor. I was a successful captain with a sterling reputation.\nUntil...\nThose cursed sea giants ruined me! They smashed my ship, killed my crew, and set me on a lifeboat to Booty Bay. And one of the giants, Gorlash, stole my Captain's Chest. He said he wanted it for a snuffbox. The nerve!\nI hear Gorlash wanders the coast east of here. Find him and get back my chest! Do that, and you'll have earned a captain's gratitude.","rew":"You will receive:\nBloodband Bracers\nExperience: 3,150\n+75 reputation with Booty Bay\n-375 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Ahoy, ‹name›! Did you find Gorlash? That chest was my favorite, and it has a hidden compartment that held my greatest treasures!","done":"You found it! Oh happy day, this is! Thank you, ‹name›. Getting back my chest cools some of the fire in me.\nBut my revenge isn't complete...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.7,"y":73.6,"n":"Captain Hecklebury Smotts","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8071":{"id":8071,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Confessor's Mantle","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Aegis. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.\nAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Aegis\nReach 21000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"The confessors of the Zandalar all wear a distinctive mantle, marking them as the preservers of the tribe. These mantles are woven with powerful mojo that aids them in judging those who would threaten our tribe. As a priest, you too must spend your time judging those worthy and not; such a mantle would definitely be a blessing to you.\nIn exchange for fighting Hakkar's minions in Zul'Gurub and bringing me the Paragons of Power I seek, I will give you a mantle worthy of our finest confessors.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Confessor's Mantle\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Do you have the Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub?","done":"Well done, ‹name› - the minions of Hakkar have surely felt the retribution of the Zandalar today, thanks to you. Your actions have given you a permanent place of reverence within the tribe. With our blessing, please take this confessor's mantle as your own!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"871":{"id":871,"t":"Disrupt the Attacks","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Of the Razormane tribe, kill 8 Water Seekers, 8 Thornweavers and 3 Hunters, and then return to Thork in the Crossroads.\nRazormane Water Seeker slain : 0/ 8\nRazormane Thornweaver slain : 0/ 8\nRazormane Hunter slain : 0/ 3","desc":"All the quilboars are our enemies, ‹name›. Some just prove to be more of a nuisance than others.\nThe Razormane tribe has been attacking our supply lines from Durotar, causing us no end of annoyance. I have scouts seeking the leader of these raids, but until then, any losses you can inflict on the filthy pig men would aid us.\nStart in the northeast towards Durotar. You can always tell their dens from the huge thorny vines that come up from the earth. Seek them out, and slay them.","rew":"Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"The longer it takes to stop these attacks, the harder it will be to provide supplies for the people of the Crossroads.","done":"You have done well, ‹name›. Those insolent quilboars will finally learn that the might of the Horde is not to be ignored.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.5,"y":30.9,"n":"Thork","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"391":{"id":391,"t":"The Stockade Riots","lv":29,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 4,950 experience instead of 2,650, 1.87 times as much. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Kill Bazil Thredd and bring his head back to Warden Thelwater at the Stockade.\nHead of Bazil Thredd Bazil Thredd","desc":"Let's get one thing straight, ‹name›: I don't trust you. But, with the situation as it is, you probably won't make a difference.\nSo here's how it's going to be: go down there and have your talk with Thredd. If you're really on our side, then kill him and bring me his head when the job's done. And if it turns out you're on his side, and don't come out... when we find you, you'll die along with the rest of the maggots.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,950\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Either you bring me Thredd's head, or I'll take yours, understand, ‹name›?","done":"Without Thredd to lead them, hopefully the riots will be more controllable. We shall see.\nI must say, after a half hour, I hardly expected you to come out, but it seems I misjudged you.\nI'd guess, then, that you didn't get much useful information out of him? But I know a thing or two that might be of interest to you about Thredd's activities.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.5,"y":69.4,"n":"Warden Thelwater","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-stockade"]},"1111":{"id":1111,"t":"Wharfmaster Dizzywig","lv":36,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Kravel's Parts Order to Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet.\nKravel's Parts Order\nProvided: Kravel's Parts Order","desc":"I make it my job to get people what they need, and the gnomes over there need a parts order filled. Their parts were shipped to Ratchet a week ago, but I haven't been able to make the trip.\nSo, are you ready for some legwork? Go to Ratchet and give this parts order to Wharfmaster Dizzywig -- he'll probably be at the docks.\nDo this for me, and I'll have more jobs for you.\nJobs, my friend, with serious profit potential...","rew":"Experience: 1,400","back":"Speak up! Tell me, are you dropping off or picking up?","done":"Oh yes. Parts for Kravel. I'm glad you're here. These things have been sitting out here for days, and I was afraid they'd rust!\nThousand Needles The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.8,"y":77.3,"n":"Kravel Koalbeard","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":63.4,"y":38.5,"n":"Wharfmaster Dizzywig","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1191":{"id":1191,"t":"Zamek's Distraction","lv":41,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","done":"Let's go!","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":79.8,"y":77,"n":"Zamek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1511":{"id":1511,"t":"Ken'zigla's Draught","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ken'zigla's Draught to Grunt Logmar at Camp Taurajo.\nKen'zigla's Draught\nProvided: Ken'zigla's Draught","desc":"I figured there might be another coming to get the draught, so I prepared it anyways.\nHere you go, ‹name›. Mind you, you should only give half of it to him! That will give him enough strength to move without bleeding himself dry. Wait a night, then give him the other half.\nAnyways, you'll want to bring this to Logmar at Camp Taurajo. From what the first one told me, he should have an idea where this Dogran is.","rew":"Experience: 1,550","back":"Yes, what is it?","done":"Well, it's about time! Dogran has been dying out there, waiting for this.\nWe need to get this out to him right away, but most of the grunts stationed here are out on a foraging mission.\nStonetalon Mountains The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":73.2,"y":95.1,"n":"Ken'zigla","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.6,"y":59.3,"n":"Grunt Logmar","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"5511":{"id":5511,"t":"The Key to Scholomance","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nSkeleton Key\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Undercity","done":"Well, here you are, ‹name› - the completed Skeleton Key. I am certain as I can be that this key will allow you within the confines of the Scholomance. There's only one way to be absolutely sure it works, though. Waste no time in trying it out, I say.\nGood luck, mighty hero. May your victories continue to bring you fame and power as you lay waste to Scholomance!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.1,"y":68.9,"n":"High Executor Derrington","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"151":{"id":151,"t":"Poor Old Blanchy","lv":14,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Verna Furlbrow in Westfall wants you to bring her 8 Handfuls of Oats.\n8 Handful of Oats Sack of Oats , Noggle's Satchel","desc":"Poor Old Blanchy! Such a tired beast after all the work we put her through. I fed her before we left the farm, but we weren't expecting the wagon to break on us. If you could bring her a few handfuls of oats from the fields, I'd be grateful.\nI bet you could find some around all of the farms in Westfall, if you can steer clear of those horrific machines that have taken over. There are several farms southwest of here.","rew":"You will receive:\nOld Blanchy's Blanket Old Blanchy's Feed Pouch\nExperience: 1,250\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Old Blanchy is on her last leg. Did you happen to find any oats for her?","done":"Thank you so much, ‹name›! Poor Old Blanchy will be so happy!","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":59.9,"y":19.4,"n":"Verna Furlbrow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"471":{"id":471,"t":"Apprentice's Duties","lv":26,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 6 Giant Crocolisk Skins and bring them to James Halloran in Menethil Harbor.\n6 Giant Crocolisk Skin Giant Wetlands Crocolisk 80 %","desc":"I sent my apprentice out into the marshes to skin some of our famous giant Wetlands crocolisks. When he didn't return, I went out to look for him... Let's just say it wasn't a pretty sight.\nMidwife says he might pull through, but in the meantime I still need my skins!\n...If you'd like to kill a few more of the brutes, I wouldn't be opposed, after what they did. You'll find the crocs north up the coast, beyond the murloc hovels.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMalleable Chain Leggings Resilient Poncho\nYou will also receive:\nRecipe: Crocolisk Gumbo\nExperience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"My apprentice is like a son to me. It's going to be hard for him to live his life with only one leg.\nAh, ‹name›, how goes it? Do you have my skins?","done":"Hmm... Don't suppose you'd be interested in becoming my apprentice, would you?\nHah! No, I'm just kidding. You're much too old, for one thing. Besides - from the looks of you, it would seem that you have other ambitions in life. Nonetheless, these are some fine skins you've procured, and I'll be able to put them to good use.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":8.5,"y":55.7,"n":"James Halloran","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"631":{"id":631,"t":"The Thandol Span","lv":31,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rhag Garmason wants you to locate Ol' Rustlocke.","desc":"A tremendous explosion roared through the hills. 'Twas horrible, I tell you!\nGood soldiers died defending the Thandol Span. Longbraid says we'll take revenge on the Dark Irons before all is said and done.\nWe're in a world of hurt though and I don't see any reinforcements in sight. Longbraid sent Ol' Rustlocke to scout the eastern bridge to see if we could secure it.\nThat was days ago. We haven't the manpower to search for him with Dun Modr under siege.\nPerhaps you can find him...","rew":"Experience: 2,500\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","done":"You search the tiny, dwarven corpse. Engraved into the helmet you can clearly read: Ebenezer Rustlocke.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.9,"y":18.2,"n":"Rhag Garmason","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":51.3,"y":8,"n":"Ebenezer Rustlocke's Corpse","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"8471":{"id":8471,"t":"Winterfall Ritual Totem","lv":56,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Winterfall Ritual Totem inside Timbermaw Hold and see if one of the furbolgs there will find a use for the item. The Timbermaw will not speak with you unless you are of Neutral reputation or greater with them.\nWinterfall Ritual Totem Winterfall Totemic 4 % , Winterfall Runner 3.2 % , Winterfall Pathfinder 3.2 % , Winterfall Den Watcher 3.1 % and 3 more\nReach 0 reputation with Timbermaw Hold\nProvided: Winterfall Ritual Totem","desc":"You have found one of the Winterfall furbolg's ritual totems. The totem itself is of non-descript construction, but it seems to emanate an almost tangible sense of dread and despair. If many of the Winterfall furbolgs do indeed carry these, it certainly would go a long way in explaining their current condition.\nOne of the furbolgs inside Timbermaw Hold may have a use for such an item... that is, if you've earned their trust enough for them to speak with you.","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Major Healing Potion 3 Major Mana Potion\nMoney: 1 70 1 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,800\n+150 reputation with Timbermaw Hold","back":"‹class› - you approach us in a peaceful manner, but I sense that you are here on matters that are grave and severe... for both furbolg and ‹race› alike. What have you come to tell us?","done":"This thing... it is in the shape of a Winterfall Ritual Totem, but it has been twisted by forces I cannot begin to comprehend. Whatever taint that has set the Winterfall against us is surely present in this object.\nDivine wisdom has brought both this and you to us, ‹name›. We will study this object intently; perhaps one day, the Winterfall will rage against us no longer.\nThank you, friend please accept these offerings in exchange for your benevolence.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":65.5,"y":3.5,"n":"Kernda","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92471":{"id":92471,"t":"Aetheen of the gales","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Aetheen of the Gales in Thendal Grove.","desc":"You may not realize this but everything you've done has been a trial of sorts. A test for what is to come for you. It's a big island out there, and Zephras needs spirited young adventurers such as yourself if we are to survive the trials our people face.\nThe one called Aetheen of the Gales is one of the leaders of our people here on Zephras Isle, and she has been watching you. She has a task that you must complete. Speak with her to learn more.","done":"Rorian has told me much of you. I am likely unknown to you, but I am a member of the Council of Elders here on Zephras Isle. I've come to read the flow of the winds here in Thendal Grove. I'm also here to assess young shen'dorei such as yourself that are coming of age.\nSo tell me, are you ready to take your next step? Are you ready to serve Zephras Isle?","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42,"y":23.4,"n":"Rorian the Dayseeker","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42.6,"y":23.6,"n":"Aetheen of the Gales","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92551":{"id":92551,"t":"Stolen supplies","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 10 packs of Stolen Shen'dar Supplies from Falaath Village in the Shen'dar Highlands.\n10 Stolen Shen'dar Supplies","desc":"I overheard you might be going to Falaath Village? While you are there, please keep an eye out for our stolen supply caches.\nThe Al'Aketh have been raiding our supply caravans carrying various goods such as food and windstones to and from the lowlands for months. They've been blaming the bandits, of course, but we all know that it all ends up in the same place. If there's any of that stuff left in Falaath, it would be a huge help if you could recover it.","rew":"Money: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 525\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"There's a lot of hungry and desperate skyborne here who need these supplies.","done":"This is great! We've been barely squeaking by without our regular supply deliveries. I'll work with the constable to ensure that these supplies get redistributed to the townsfolk who are in most dire need.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.2,"y":45.2,"n":"Danarii Bellowveil","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92871":{"id":92871,"t":"In service of zephras","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Report to Valennia Stormfist and let her know that the Windshapers are with them in their fight against the Al'Aketh.","desc":"Valennia Stormfist and her peacekeepers have ever been the protectors of Zephras, and we've done our best to lend aid where we can. There's rumors of larger-scale cult movements around the island, and they are clearly gearing up for something.\nReport to Valennia and reiterate to her that the Windshapers offer their full support in Valanaar's efforts against the Al'Aketh, should the need arise.","done":"You seem eager to lend aid immediately. Come, let's speak further on the current situation.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59,"y":79.6,"n":"Ayessa Dawnsinger","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});